<%# The facts about the REPOSITORY rather than about a run: who owns it, how many runs it holds and —
    for a member — what they may do here, with the way out. Rendered with the Runs section once runs
    exist, and on its own on a repository CI has never reached: a member of an empty repository holds
    the same access and the same right to leave, and an absence here would read as "never granted". %>
<div id="repository-facts" class="space-y-3">
<% viewer_access = repository_policy.grantable_permissions unless repository_policy.can?(:owner) %>
<%# "Searchable intents" is NOT a test count, and never sits unlabelled beside the suite figures: it
    counts the intent rows SpecGuard has stored and can search, and is structurally 0 until the
    embedding pipeline ships (ingestion writes no spec_intents row yet). It belongs here, with the
    repository-level counts, rather than beside the verdict card's run figures — where, unlabelled
    above a non-zero "Carrying an @intent", it read as a second, contradictory description of the
    same suite. %>
<%= render UI::DefListComponent.new(rows: [["Owner", @repository.user.display_name],
                                           ["Test runs", number_with_delimiter(@repository.test_runs.count)],
                                           ["Searchable intents", number_with_delimiter(@repository.spec_intents.count)],
                                           *(viewer_access ? [["Your access", viewer_access.join(", ")]] : [])]) %>
<p class="text-xs text-app-content-secondary">
  Annotated tests SpecGuard has stored for search — not a count of tests in the suite, and
  not the denominator of anything above. Ingestion does not write these yet.
</p>
<% if viewer_access %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <p class="text-xs text-app-content-secondary"><%= held_access_description(viewer_access) %></p>
    <%= button_to "Leave", leave_repository_members_path(@repository), method: :delete,
                  class: UI::ButtonComponent.classes(variant: :danger, size: :xs),
                  form: { data: { turbo_confirm: leave_confirmation(@repository, @viewer_keys_minted) } } %>
  </div>
<% end %>
</div>
